      "content": "Continuing with managed conservation represents a dangerous, intellectually lazy reliance on outdated control narratives that actively obstruct natural planetary healing. By continually intervening, we ignore robust ecological science, effectively treating symptoms rather than addressing systemic breakdown. This human-centric micromanagement is ultimately harmful, as it prevents ecosystems from achieving their own necessary, complex trajectories toward robustness. We must urgently pivot to rewilding to honor ecological integrity rather than perpetuate flawed control mechanisms.",
      "source": "target",
